  PROJECT:&nbsp;&nbsp;Lowline Area Burned Fence Construction Project -GMUG NF in Gunnison County,&nbsp;Colorado  

   *****     11/23/2026:&nbsp; POSTING of AMENDMENT ONE - SEE&nbsp;&nbsp;(A0001_LOWLINE FENCE in Attachments/Links     *******   

  POC&#39;S: JANICE KING, CONTRACT SPECIALIST, at janice.king@usda.gov and LUCAS DAHLMAN, 
CONGTRACTING OFFICER, at lucas.dahlman@usda.gov  

   Quotes  shall be submitted via email to Janice&nbsp;King at janice.king@usda.gov and to Lucas&nbsp;Dahlman at lucas.dahlman@usda.gov no later than&nbsp;December 8, 2026, at 9:00 a.m. Mountain Time.&nbsp; This date has been extended and updated to allow sufficient time for bid submissions. Due to the the close proximity of this date, additional questions may not be answered.&nbsp;  

   DESCRIPTION:   The project will consist of constructing approximately 16,414 feet of&nbsp;four wire fence in the vicinity of the 2023 Low Line Fire, Gunnison County,&nbsp;Colorado. The purpose and need are to replace existing fences damaged by the 2023&nbsp;Low Line Fire with a friendly wildlife fence and provide removal of old and damaged&nbsp;fence materials. See the SOW, SOI, SPECS and Diagram for more details.&nbsp; 

 There was a   Site Visit   held for this project for November 9, 2026, at 10:00 a.m.Mountain Time.   Questions regarding the site visit and future visits may be found in the Questions and Answers in this Amendment. See A0001_Lowline Fence.&nbsp;   

